# SPDX-License-Identifier: MPL-2.0
#
# .hypatia-ignore — scoped, documented exemptions for the Hypatia scanner.
#
# Format (one entry per line):
#     <rule_module>/<rule_type>:<path-fragment>
#     <rule_module>/*:<path-fragment>          (any type in module)
#     <path-fragment>                           (any rule, any module)
#
# Lines starting with `#` are comments. A path-fragment is a substring match
# against the repo-relative file path. Built-in defaults live in Hypatia's
# lib/hypatia/scanner_suppression.ex — do not duplicate them here. Each entry
# below carries a stated reason. Prefer fix-the-code or an inline directive
# over an entry here; this file is for whole-file/directory exemptions.

# ─── build/docs-seed/ describes DOWNSTREAM repos, not this one ─────────────
#
# `build/docs-seed/` is the canonical template of documentation that gets
# copied into scaffolded repos. Its example paths (e.g. `src/middleware/…`,
# `src/main.rs`) describe a hypothetical generated project, so they
# legitimately do not resolve against this template's own tree. SD022
# (stale `src/<dir>/` reference) is therefore a structural false positive
# for everything under this directory — mirrors the built-in CHANGELOG.md
# and third_party/ carve-outs. Scaffolded repos inherit this file, so the
# exemption travels with the template.
structural_drift/SD022:build/docs-seed/

# ─── workflow research-extension findings ─────────────────────────────────────
#
# RE001 currently reports `warn`, while the standards workflow pinned by this
# repository accepts only critical/high/medium/low/info severities. These jobs
# deliberately use credentials for their outbound GitHub, SMTP, or analysis
# operations; exempt the affected files until that scanner/consumer contract
# converges rather than treating valid scanner output as corrupt JSON.
research_extensions/RE001:.github/workflows/boj-build.yml
research_extensions/RE001:.github/workflows/dependabot-automerge.yml
research_extensions/RE001:.github/workflows/label-triage.yml
research_extensions/RE001:.github/workflows/labels.yml
research_extensions/RE001:.github/workflows/push-email-notify.yml
research_extensions/RE001:.github/workflows/release.yml
research_extensions/RE001:.github/workflows/sonarqube.yml

# RE005's matches are intentional best-effort probes and annotation renderers,
# not test or gate commands. Their callers consume optional output or preserve
# the authoritative failure decision in a separate step.
research_extensions/RE005:.github/workflows/quality.yml
research_extensions/RE005:.github/workflows/security-policy.yml
research_extensions/RE005:.github/workflows/static-analysis-gate.yml
research_extensions/RE005:.github/workflows/wellknown-enforcement.yml

# This workflow uses the `pull_request` event and requires both the triggering
# actor and the immutable PR author to be Dependabot. RE008's spoofable-actor
# case applies to actor-only trust gates on `pull_request_target`, not this job.
research_extensions/RE008:.github/workflows/dependabot-automerge.yml
